      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $E$ into the matrix $F$, where\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nF=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $1$st row is the same in both matrices. The only rows that have changed are the $2$nd row and the $3$rd row.   \n\nBy considering the given row operations that change both the $2$nd and the $3$rd row, we notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}E & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}\u2194{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 8 & -3 & 7\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =F.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}\u2194{R}_{3}.\n$$"
