      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $W$, where\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nW=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $1$st row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $1$st row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\,{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5\\cdot {R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -5 & -10 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 10 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =W.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{3}.\n$$"
