      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $X$ into the matrix $Y$, where\n\n$$\nX=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 16 & -12 \\\\ 1 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $1$st and the $3$rd rows are the same in both matrices. The only row that has changed is the $2$nd row. \n\nBy considering the given row operations that modify the $2$nd row, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -8 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:=(-2)\\cdot {R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 & -5 \\\\ -4 & 16 & -12 \\\\ 1 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =Y.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:=(-2)\\cdot {R}_{2}.\n$$"
