      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-130098",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following elementary row operations transforms the matrix $M$ into the matrix $N$, where\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 6 & -5\\end{bmatrix},\\,N=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 6 & -5\\end{bmatrix}?\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that the $2$nd row is the same in both matrices. The only rows that have changed are the $1$st row and the $3$rd row.   \n\nBy considering the given row operations that change both the $1$st and the $3$rd row, we notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 6 & -5\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{1}\u2194{R}_{3} \\\\  & \u223c\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 6 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 7 & 6 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =N.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}\u2194{R}_{3}.\n$$"
